atlas evidence
# Harvested from the run6/run7 histories: the evidence estate the vision detailed
# as distinct calculi (do not fold into one EvidenceGraph). Registered honestly at
# architectural -- named and lineage-tracked, not yet built -- so loss() surfaces
# them as mining targets rather than losing them.

architecture artifact-graph
  canonical_name ArtifactGraph
  owns Artifact
  consumes ExecutionReceipt
  publishes Artifact
  source_path engine/core/src/fabric.c
  source_path lib/libbonfyre/src/bf_sha256.c
  witness lib/libbonfyre/tests/sha256_file_test.c verifies the shared native file hash refuses stream and close errors instead of returning a digest of a partial read
  forbidden_inference a successful shared file read -> source immutability during hashing or the subsequent artifact workflow
  family evidence
  domain Evidence / Artifacts
  layer evidence
  semantic_question What operator transformed this source artifact into that derived one?
  purpose Transformation semantics: source -> operator -> derived -> packet -> export. Distinct from lineage (ancestry) and provenance (who/what/when).
  maturity implemented
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/evidence_graphs.py.archive
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/protocol_evidence.py.archive
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_evidence_graphs.py.archive
  node_types SourceArtifact
  node_types DerivedArtifact
  edge_types transformed_by
  forbidden_inference an artifact exists -> it supports a claim
  source_lineage run6/run7 evidence estate
  known_gap content-addressing (HashIdentity) and fabric artifacts are the nearest real shapes

architecture provenance-graph
  canonical_name ProvenanceGraph
  family evidence
  domain Evidence / Provenance
  layer evidence
  semantic_question Through what source, observer, actor, runtime, model, provider, transport did this arrive?
  purpose The full path an artifact took to exist -- the cheap path-vector checks (untrusted provider, missing authority provenance, loops) ride on this.
  maturity implemented
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/evidence_graphs.py.archive
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_evidence_graphs.py.archive
  node_types ProvenanceNode
  edge_types produced_by
  forbidden_inference a provenance path -> authority over the artifact
  source_lineage run6/run7 evidence estate
  known_gap ResultReceiptBundle chain is a partial real shape
  known_gap every source this entry names is archived, so nothing here is a live implementation a reader can open and run. Whether a native owner has taken this work over is not established in this entry; until one is named and witnessed here, the architecture stands on retired code.
architecture evidence-graph
  owns Evidence
  consumes Occurrence
  consumes Artifact
  publishes Evidence
  canonical_name EvidenceGraph
  family evidence
  domain Evidence / Claims
  layer evidence
  semantic_question Does this support, contradict, reproduce, or falsify that claim?
  purpose The claim-support relation itself (supports / contradicts / reproduces / falsifies / contextualizes / witnesses). SERM produces its consequences; it is not this.
  maturity implemented
  source_path components/BonfyreControlPlane/evidence_graphs.py.archive
  source_path engine/core/src/evidence.c
  source_path engine/core/include/bf_evidence.h
  witness components/BonfyreControlPlane/tests/test_evidence_graphs.py.archive
  witness engine/core/tests/evidence_test.c
  node_types Claim
  edge_types supports
  edge_types contradicts
  forbidden_inference correlation -> causation
  invariant an evidence relation is directional: supports(A,B) never implies supports(B,A) (native + python parity on the shared evidence_relations store)
  known_gap native owner records directional supports/contradicts/reproduces/falsifies relations with kind gating and derives the precedence-ordered current verdict (falsified > contested > reproduced > supported > unevidenced) from that same relation; it never turns standing evidence into a proof-frontier verdict
  forbidden_inference supports(A,B) -> supports(B,A)
  source_lineage run6/run7 evidence estate
  known_gap EvidenceBindingGraph binds candidates, does not maintain the claim relation

architecture temporal-evidence-graph
