architecture receipt-envelope
  canonical_name ReceiptEnvelope
  owns ReceiptEnvelope
  consumes AgentEvent
  consumes Occurrence
  consumes Artifact
  publishes Evidence
  family evidence
  domain Evidence / Receipts
  layer evidence/receipt
  semantic_question What exact session event frontier occurred, and from which evidence origin and identity dimensions?
  purpose Composite receipt boundary over session events with subject/host/external origin fidelity and separately typed artifact, producer/model and transport identities.
  maturity implemented
  node_types ReceiptEnvelope
  node_types ReceiptEvidence
  edge_types covers_event
  edge_types produced_by
  edge_types carried_by
  invariant receipt coverage requires same-sequence and same-origin evidence for every AgentEvent
  invariant model-turn evidence repeats the exact provider and model identity declared by the covered event and binds an explicit producer verifier observation
  invariant the carrier adapter accepts bounded explicit fields for provider-native session identity, context compaction, strategy transition, artifact identity and external transport identity; absent fields are refused when their event/origin kind requires them and never filled from a process exit
  invariant external evidence carries transport identity while artifact, producer/model and transport identities remain orthogonal
  forbidden_inference artifact/content identity -> producer, model, transport, authority, provenance, or claim support
  forbidden_inference repeated provider/model attribution -> verified producer fidelity without a verifier observation
  forbidden_inference subject, host, or external origin -> either of the other origin classes
  source_path schemas/control/agent-session-receipt.yaff
  source_path engine/core/src/agent_contract.c
  source_path engine/core/include/bf_agent_contract.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreAgentContract/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreActors/tests/organ_callers_test.sh
  witness engine/core/tests/agent_contract_test.c
  witness cmd/BonfyreActors/tests/organ_callers_test.sh proves the native caller accepts a same-origin, same-sequence model-turn receipt only when its provider/model identities and verifier observation cover the declared session frontier
  witness cmd/BonfyreAgentContract/tests/receipt_frontier_test.sh proves one receipt covers a contiguous model-turn, context-compaction, strategy-change and external model-turn frontier, while an external event without transport identity is refused
  source_lineage V8.1 ReceiptEnvelope and Run8 cross-provider identity review
  known_gap the native caller validates explicit session files; no standing worker has yet been bound to emit its own AgentSession and ReceiptEnvelope through this contract.
architecture running-system-attestation
  canonical_name RunningSystemAttestation
  owns RunningSystemClaim
  consumes Artifact
  publishes Evidence
  family evidence
  domain Evidence / Deployment
  layer evidence/attestation
  semantic_question Which bytes were sealed, which are deployed, and which are actually executing right now?
  purpose Separates three claims that are routinely spoken as one. A sealed release is bytes someone committed to; a deployed artifact is what sits at the path a unit names; a running artifact is the inode the kernel is executing. Replacing a file without restarting leaves the process on the old, now-unlinked inode while every health surface reports healthy. Reads the release's existing sha256 manifest rather than introducing a second attestation format.
  maturity implemented
  node_types SealedArtifact
  node_types DeployedArtifact
  node_types RunningArtifact
  edge_types deployed_from
  edge_types executing
  invariant the question asked matches the artifact kind: an ELF is compared by content through /proc/<pid>/exe, while an interpreted unit executes its interpreter and is compared by whether its source changed after the process started
  invariant running-differs-from-deployed fails the check, and deployed-differs-from-sealed only reports; a check that fails during ordinary development is a check that gets ignored
  forbidden_inference a service reporting active -> the service executing the bytes on disk (a replaced file leaves the process on the unlinked inode, and every health surface still answers)
  forbidden_inference sealed, deployed and running agreeing -> the bytes being correct, tested or authorized (this settles which bytes, never whether they are right)
  forbidden_inference a version endpoint or deploy log -> evidence of what is executing (both report intent; only the running inode reports fact)
  source_path scripts/release_attest.mjs
  source_path scripts/release_attest.py.archive
  source_path scripts/release_metadata.mjs
  source_path scripts/tests/release_attest_test.mjs
  witness scripts/tests/release_attest_test.mjs proves an env-wrapped Bun service attests its script rather than its interpreter or an argument binary, and that running-byte drift and a changed interpreted source are fatal while deployed-versus-sealed drift remains reported
  source_path scripts/deploy_organ.sh
  source_path scripts/seal_release.sh
  witness scripts/release_attest.py proved detection against a live estate: touching an interpreted unit's source without restarting reported SOURCE_CHANGED_SINCE_START and exited 1, and the same estate returned to exit 0 after a restart
  witness scripts/deploy_organ.sh refuses a broken change with exit 2 and leaves the live binary byte-identical and serving 200; a good change exits 0; a probe returning other than the expected status exits 1
  invariant a deploy builds, installs only bytes that build produced, restarts, attests the running inode and probes a real route; each step fails closed, because the hand-rolled sequence it replaces piped make into grep and installed the stale binary still on disk
  invariant the artifact a unit executes is the last existing path token of its final ExecStart, never the first: for an interpreter plus a script the script is the artifact, and denylisting interpreter names by hand resolved the oauth unit to /usr/bin/node and compared node against node
  invariant sealing refuses while any unit runs bytes other than the deployed ones, and excludes backup copies; certifying drift or freezing which of two similar binaries is real are both worse than leaving the question open
  witness scripts/seal_release.sh sealed 116 artifacts including 8 unit entrypoints, excluding 20 backup copies, after which all three attested units report deployed equal to sealed and running equal to deployed
  known_gap the seal covers what is deployed, not what built it: a sealed organ cannot be rebuilt from the manifest alone, because source hashes are not recorded beside the binary hashes

architecture witness-mutation
  canonical_name WitnessMutation
  family evidence
  domain Evidence
  maturity measured
  semantic_question If a declared fact were wrong, would anything in this institution notice?
  # The atlas forbids maturity laundering and has enforced it as "a witness
  # exists and can be opened". That is not the rule. The rule is that the witness
  # would notice if the thing it witnesses were false, and nothing here had ever
  # checked it.
  #
  # A passing suite proves nothing alone. A suite that passes and then goes red
  # the moment a fact it claims to check is changed underneath it has proven it
  # is load-bearing. That difference is the whole difference between a test and
  # a decoration.
  node_types DeclaredFact
  node_types Witness
  edge_types defends
  state_types guarded
  state_types blind
  state_types inconclusive
  invariant every suite must pass before any fact is mutated; a suite already red cannot demonstrate that it noticed, and counting it as guarded would be the laundering this exists to detect
  invariant a suite that skips is not a suite that passed; several exit zero on an empty world, so a mutation that makes the world unfindable would otherwise record the field as undefended -- the tool manufacturing the finding it exists to detect
  invariant the mutation keeps the shape of the value it replaces, because a number turned into a word is caught by a type check rather than by anything that understands the field
  invariant a fingerprint pins values and not counts; counting how many cash deltas are known left 0.00 becoming 1.0 invisible, and that a vendor term supplies exactly zero is the entire finding it was meant to defend
  forbidden_inference a guarded field -> a correct value; the suite reacted to a change, which says nothing about whether the original was right
  forbidden_inference a blind field -> an untested one; only that no suite run here reacted
  forbidden_inference a passing suite -> a load-bearing one, until it has gone red for a reason
  computational_form search
  native_format json
  source_path scripts/witness_mutation.mjs
  witness scripts/witness_mutation.test.mjs
  invariant mutation plans declare PURE effect class and argv arrays; arbitrary shell command strings, source-store writes, and implicit execution are refused
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/capital_transform_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/closure_algebra_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/funding_closure_test.sh
  invariant a fact whose change moves no computed answer anywhere is inert and no witness is faulted for missing it; 241 of 284 are, and reporting them as gaps would drown eleven real ones in noise
  invariant a producer is run twice on the untouched store before anything is mutated, and any key differing between those two runs is excluded; representation_trial carries a trials block that moves on its own, and with it counted every mutation looked load-bearing and every guard graded a consequence
  measured 284 declared facts across all 29 populated content types were each changed to a plausible wrong value with eight suites watching: 241 inert, 26 guarded, 17 blind
  measured 17 facts changed what the institution computes while every suite stayed green, including a budget request's amount, what a funding route satisfies, and a resolver's success probability set to 2.2 -- a number outside [0,1] that the algebra went on multiplying by
  measured of the 26 guards, 23 held because a computed answer moved and 2 only because a declaration fingerprint was pinned; a fingerprint guard detects tampering and is no evidence the field does any work
  measured after adding consequence assertions and refusing impossible declarations the same 284 mutations give 32 guarded and 11 blind, with 6 named facts moved from computing-differently-unnoticed to defended
  known_gap 11 facts still move a computed answer with no suite reacting, and 23 of the 61 architectures claiming measured rest on a witness file nothing in this estate runs
